          "text": "U.S. Ambassador to Israel: There’s no such thing as replacement theology, because to think that means God would break his promise!!\n\nSo what exactly is replacement theology?🤔\n\nReplacement theology, also called supersessionism, is the Christian doctrine that the Church has permanently replaced ethnic Israel as God’s chosen people.\n\nIn this view, covenant promises in the Hebrew Bible no longer belong uniquely to the Jewish people, but have been transferred to the Christian Church. ✝️\n\nSupporters traditionally argued that because many Jewish people did not accept Jesus as Messiah, God’s covenant promises passed from Israel to the Church, making the Church the new Israel.\n\nAnd the debate reaches beyond theology. Critics argue replacement theology helped fuel centuries of antisemitism by portraying Jews as rejected or stripped of covenant status.🤨\n\n Opponents believe affirming God’s continuing promises to Israel can strengthen Jewish-Christian relations and reshape how Christians discuss Israel today.\n\nSo where do you stand?\nCan God's covenant be transferred from one people to another, or does it remain everlasting?🤔\n\nSubscribe to @TruthTrumpPost  for more  videos like these."
